First Author: Xia
Title: Machine Learning for Predicting Primary Graft Dysfunction After Lung Transplantation: An Interpretable Model Study
Source number: 80

Very short summary: This retrospective single-center study included 802 adult lung transplant recipients treated in China between July 2018 and October 2023, comprising a 640-patient derivation cohort and a later 162-patient temporal external-validation cohort. Nine machine-learning algorithms were compared after logistic-regression and LASSO feature selection; Random Forest performed best, achieving an external-validation AUC of 0.8214, accuracy of 76.54%, sensitivity of 82.35%, specificity of 66.67%, and F1-score of 0.8155 for grade 3 primary graft dysfunction within 72 hours.

