	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Patients with severe missingness were excluded, defined as missing any key variable or more than 20% of other variables. Remaining missing data were filled using K-nearest-neighbour imputation. The 640-patient derivation cohort was split 7:3 into 448 training and 192 internal-validation patients, and the independent later temporal cohort contained 162 patients. PGD3 prevalence was 36.4% in derivation and 37.0% externally, but no class weighting, over-sampling, under-sampling, or other explicit imbalance method was reported. Source code and trained model weights were not reported.

